&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style="font-family:arial nova,arial nova_embeddedfont,arial nova_msfontservice,sans-serif; font-size:12pt"&gt;OREGON CITY&amp;nbsp;&mdash; Clackamas Community College, in partnership with the Community Legal and Educational Access and Referral (CLEAR) Clinic, is hosting a free&amp;nbsp;tenant rights&amp;nbsp;presentation&amp;nbsp;to inform community members about their rights as tenants under Oregon law.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family:arial nova,arial nova_embeddedfont,arial nova_msfontservice,sans-serif; font-size:12pt"&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;

&lt;div class="OutlineElement Ltr SCXW70747292 BCX8" style="-webkit-user-drag: none; -webkit-tap-highlight-color: transparent; margin: 0px; padding: 0px; user-select: text; clear: both; cursor: text; overflow: visible; position: relative; direction: ltr; font-family: &amp;quot;Segoe UI&amp;quot;, &amp;quot;Segoe UI Web&amp;quot;, Arial, Verdana, sans-serif; font-size: 12px; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255);"&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style="font-family:arial nova,arial nova_embeddedfont,arial nova_msfontservice,sans-serif; font-size:12pt"&gt;Tenant&rsquo;s Rights 101 will be held Wednesday, Feb. 4,&amp;nbsp;noon to 1 p.m.,&amp;nbsp;in&amp;nbsp;the&amp;nbsp;Wacheno Welcome Center, Start Lab Room 151, on the college&rsquo;s Oregon City campus,&amp;nbsp;located&amp;nbsp;at 19600 Molalla Ave. Parking is free, and all are welcome to attend.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family:arial nova,arial nova_embeddedfont,arial nova_msfontservice,sans-serif; font-size:12pt"&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;

&lt;div class="OutlineElement Ltr SCXW70747292 BCX8" style="-webkit-user-drag: none; -webkit-tap-highlight-color: transparent; margin: 0px; padding: 0px; user-select: text; clear: both; cursor: text; overflow: visible; position: relative; direction: ltr; font-family: &amp;quot;Segoe UI&amp;quot;, &amp;quot;Segoe UI Web&amp;quot;, Arial, Verdana, sans-serif; font-size: 12px; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255);"&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style="font-family:arial nova,arial nova_embeddedfont,arial nova_msfontservice,sans-serif; font-size:12pt"&gt;Presenters from the CLEAR Clinic will provide an overview of Oregon landlord and tenant laws, including topics such as rental agreements, security deposits, rent increases, fees and utilities, maintenance and habitability, termination notices, and&amp;nbsp;special circumstances&amp;nbsp;such as domestic violence. The&amp;nbsp;session&amp;nbsp;is designed to empower tenants with knowledge and resources to understand what landlords can and cannot do.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family:arial nova,arial nova_embeddedfont,arial nova_msfontservice,sans-serif; font-size:12pt"&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;

&lt;div class="OutlineElement Ltr SCXW70747292 BCX8" style="-webkit-user-drag: none; -webkit-tap-highlight-color: transparent; margin: 0px; padding: 0px; user-select: text; clear: both; cursor: text; overflow: visible; position: relative; direction: ltr; font-family: &amp;quot;Segoe UI&amp;quot;, &amp;quot;Segoe UI Web&amp;quot;, Arial, Verdana, sans-serif; font-size: 12px; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255);"&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style="font-family:arial nova,arial nova_embeddedfont,arial nova_msfontservice,sans-serif; font-size:12pt"&gt;The CLEAR Clinic offers legal information and referrals to underserved communities in the Portland metro area. Staffed by legal professionals and trained volunteers, the clinic provides accessible, no-cost support to help individuals understand and navigate civil legal issues.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family:arial nova,arial nova_embeddedfont,arial nova_msfontservice,sans-serif; font-size:12pt"&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;

