&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style="font-family:arial,helvetica,sans-serif"&gt;&lt;span style="font-size:11pt"&gt;VANCOUVER, Wash.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-size:14.666667px"&gt;&mdash;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-size:11pt"&gt;&amp;nbsp;Clark College hosted three full days of big band jazz at the Annual Clark College Jazz Festival, where s&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="color:black; font-size:11pt"&gt;ixty middle and high school jazz ensembles from throughout Washington and Oregon performed in this year&rsquo;s competition.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="color:black; font-size:11pt"&gt;Trophies were presented to the top three jazz ensembles for middle schools and division A through AAAA high schools. Individual outstanding musician and outstanding section awards were also presented at the end of each division&rsquo;s preliminary competitions.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

